  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since x-axis is normal to the circle at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, and normal to the circle passes through its centre. So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is a diameter.</p><p>Now, perpendicular from centre of circle to chord bisects the chord, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Also, product of segments of chords in a circle is equal i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/632c8fcc-62ab-42c2-b093-642dc5922507-image.png\" style=\"width: 314px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>Now, area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p>",
